annotator_A_json:
{
  "annotations": [
    {
      "text": "The pictures and footage only scratch the surface of the tale: wide smiles, and the tears of joy of a mother and her son, reunited after six years.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "Six years ago, Jane Daniels, 60, from Delft, near Cape Town, South Africa , was distraught when her son, who is mentally challenged, disappeared.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "When the police came up with no leads, after three years, Denzil was presumed dead, and a memorial service was held.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "But two weeks ago, police in the neighboring country of Eswatini, formerly called Swaziland, carried out a routine stop and search of a man who was found rummaging through trash outside a supermarket.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 3
    },
    {
      "text": "He gave them an address in Delft the Daniels' home.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "The Eswatini police sent a photo of Denzil to the Cape police missing persons' unit, and Warrant Officer Michael Daniels no relation took it to Mrs. Daniels and asked her if she knew the man in the photo.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "BODY OF KENYAN STOWAWAY FOUND IN LONDON YARD AFTER FALLING FROM PLANE'S LANDING GEAR Officer Daniels didn't expect the reaction he received.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "\"My heart is going out for her. We should help this woman, because when we brought the news to say your child is in Swaziland, she just fainted,\" he said.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "But Mrs. Daniels couldn't afford to make the 2,200-mile round trip to collect her son, now 30, who was being looked after by the Eswatini police.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "Fortunately, radio and multimedia journalist Lauren Isaacs of South Africa's Eye Witness News ( EWN ) came to the rescue.",
      "category": "Exaggeration",
      "subcategory": "Exaggeration",
      "paragraphIndex": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "A Delft pastor appealed to Isaacs for help, and the reporter visited the mother.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "\"I saw the desperation on her, and her poor circumstances.,\" Isaacs told Fox News.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "\"For three days I called businesses begging for money\".",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "\"In 90% of missing persons cases, it doesn't end well. It gets to us, I needed to get help for this family.\"",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "POLITICIAN'S $13 MILLION SUPERCAR STASH SEIZED IN CORRUPTIONS PROBES TO BE AUCTIONED FOR CHARITY NIGERIAN INVESTIGATORS DISMISS WILD REPORTS ROGUE GORILLA ATE $22G IN CASH AT ZOO, PIN MISSING MONEY ON ARMED ROBBERS The reporter also called humanitarian aid group the Gift of the Givers, who not only agreed to become the main funders of the trip, but even provided the son with new clothes.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "There are no direct road transport links between Eswatini and Cape Town.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "So Warrant Officer Daniels and a police colleague took vacation time, and used the policeman's private car for the two-day journey to reunite mother and son at the border.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 16
    },
    {
      "text": "On seeing her son, Jane repeatedly hugged him and kept saying: \"My son, my son, I am so happy to see you.\"",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 17
    },
    {
      "text": "Denzil for his part said he had hitchhiked to Eswatini where he made friends and did odd jobs to make a living.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 18
    },
    {
      "text": "\"I helped people to earn some money, selling clothes and stuff like that... I missed my family.\"",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 19
    },
    {
      "text": "He later explained to News24.com : \"I wasn't actually going to Swaziland. I was in Wellington and then I moved further and further.\"",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 20
    },
    {
      "text": "He added that he now hopes to find work and act as the family's breadwinner after his father died two years ago.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 21
    },
    {
      "text": "CLICK HERE FOR THE FOX NEWS APP Officer Daniels said he'd go the extra thousands of miles again in his car in a heartbeat:",
      "category": "Exaggeration",
      "subcategory": "Exaggeration",
      "paragraphIndex": 22
    },
    {
      "text": "\"People are very negative about the police, but there are good police officers who go out of their way to help the community\".",
      "category": "Causal Oversimplification",
      "subcategory": "Causal Oversimplification",
      "paragraphIndex": 23
