annotator_A_json:
{
  "annotations": [
    {
      "text": "Damage to the earth's crust from the 6.4 and 7.1 magnitude earthquakes that struck Southern California last week is visible in a kaleidoscopic satellite image released by NASA.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "The Advanced Rapid Imaging and Analysis team at NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory in Pasadena, California, used satellite data to produce a map showing ruptures and displacements not visible to the naked eye employing technology that has been developed over the last quarter century.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "The imagery was acquired on July 8 and compared with data from April 8.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "The earthquakes were the largest to hit California in nearly 20 years and were felt as far away as Phoenix and Mexicali, Mexico.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "The temblors and the thousands of aftershocks that followed did not lead to major structural damage near the Ridgecrest epicenter, but did have residents of nearby Trona, Calif. worrying about their town's future.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "Authorities are investigating whether the death of a man 95 miles away in Pahrump, Nev., was tied to the earthquake.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 0
    },
    {
      "text": "The man was pinned under a Jeep after the vehicle fell off its jacks following the quake.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "On the NASA map, each color of the psychedelic-looking image represents 4.8 inches of ground displacement.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Linear color lines indicate where an area was cracked open or was disturbed.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "\"One of the things that we want to know after an earthquake happens is which fault moved and how far it moved.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "So, by using these satellite images, we can determine where the fault is, what lengths of the fault slipped in the earthquake and which fault moved the most.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "That allows us to better understand where future earthquakes could happen,\" said JPL's Eric Fielding.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "It once took a year to obtain such satellite images, as was the case when capturing the impact of the 7.3 magnitude Landers earthquake in the Mojave Desert in 1992.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "But Fielding said that since 2016, images can arrive within three to four days.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "The Japanese Aerospace Exploration Agency provided the data to produce the map.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "NASA is building its own radar satellite at JPL.",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "When it launches in roughly three years, Fielding said, the technology will be able to \"map the whole Earth every 12 days.\"",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "colleen.shalby@latimes.com @cshalby",
      "category": "No Polarizing language",
      "subcategory": "no polarizing language",
      "paragraphIndex": 2
    }
  ]
}

